# The dev inspector (Step 30): copy to .env.local (gitignored, never committed) and fill in.
# Read by the dev server only (`make ui`); nothing here reaches the browser or `npm run build`.
#
# 1 shows the panel (state, transition row and reason per turn); empty hides it. `VITE_INSPECTOR=1
# make ui` does the same for one run.
VITE_INSPECTOR=1
# The Conversation API's compliance key (its SS_COMPLIANCE_API_KEY: the dev default in
# orchestrator/src/surakshasetu/config.py unless your orchestrator/.env sets another). Only
# vite.config.ts's proxy reads it, to add the Authorization header to the audit-headers read.
# Without it the panel says "not configured" and the chat works as usual.
SS_COMPLIANCE_API_KEY=surakshasetu-dev-compliance-key
